FIELD CLASS
*Field is used with Pydantic models to add validation rules, metadata, defaults, and documentation for request/response data.
*  ... in Field(...)
   ... means the field is required.
*Field class is used in model attributes of class
* path is used in path parameter and field is used in pydantic models to validate rules
from fastapi import FastAPI
import uvicorn
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field

app = FastAPI()

class Profile(BaseModel):
    name: str = Field(..., min_length=1, max_length=10)
    technology: str

@app.get("/profile/{name}/{technology")
async def get_details(name: str, technology: str):
    return {
        "name": name,
        "technology": technology
    }

if __name__ == "__main__":
    uvicorn.run("pydantic_basic:app",host="127.0.0.1",port=8080,reload=True)

* you can use the following query parameter url to access -> http://127.0.0.1:8080/profile?name=John&technology=Python  or
* If you are accessing only http://127.0.0.1:8080/profile ->you will get error because there are 2 parameters and we need to pass them also

Request Body
*To use pydantic model object as request body we need to use POST operation
* we can access this model object as request body only with docs not with URL

from fastapi import FastAPI
import uvicorn
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field

app = FastAPI()

class Profile(BaseModel):
    name: str = Field(..., min_length=1, max_length=10)
    technology: str

@app.get("/profile")
async def get_details(name: str, technology: str):
    return {
        "name": name,
        "technology": technology
    }

@app.post("/profile")
async def post_details(p:Profile):
    return p

if __name__ == "__main__":
    uvicorn.run("pydantic_basic:app",host="127.0.0.1",port=8080,reload=True)


  







